# November 28, 2026: state hospitals and asylums of Pennsylvania, a batch of the themed pass on historic asylums.
# Harrisburg State Hospital was already on the map and is left out. Fifteen institutions: the Kirkbride-plan state
# hospitals at Danville and Warren and the lost one at Dixmont; Kirkbride's own hospital in West Philadelphia and the
# Quaker asylum at Frankford; Norristown; the training schools at Pennhurst, Polk and Laurelton; the county asylums
# the state took over in 1938-1943 (Embreeville, Retreat, Mayview, Byberry); Allentown; and Farview, the state's
# hospital for the criminally insane. Most Pennsylvania state hospitals were never put on the National Register.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia's articles (and its Kirkbride Plan list); the Park Service records for
# Reed Hall at Dixmont, Kirkbride's Hospital and Friends Hospital, and the Register forms for the last two; the
# Society of Architectural Historians' Archipedia (Danville, Warren, Polk); the National Park Service's page on
# Kirkbride's Hospital; the Living New Deal (Laurelton); the Pennsylvania Department of Corrections (SCI Waymart);
# West Bradford Township's Embreeville pages; news reports (WHYY, Patch, Lehigh Valley Public Media, the Daily Item,
# the Times Leader, the Republican & Herald, Explore Jefferson, Vista.Today, TribLive); Asylum Projects for a few
# dates no other page gave (named where used); the Pennhurst attraction's own page; a waymark for the Dixmont cemetery.
# Pins: OpenStreetMap points, Wikipedia's points and ArcGIS geocoder points, each looked at on the aerial.
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
